{
  "title": "Split export_game.py (1356 lines) into focused modules",
  "description": "export_game.py mixes 7 distinct domains in one module: card metadata fetching, error log processing, LLM event aggregation, game state serialization, decision building, export assembly, and CLI.\n\nSuggested extraction targets:\n\n1. **export_card_data.py** (~200 lines) — _build_card_images, _trim_card, _collect_card_names, _build_card_data (50 lines). Scryfall API integration and card metadata collection.\n\n2. **export_llm_events.py** (~190 lines) — _read_llm_events (130+ lines), compute_thinking_time (30 lines), compute_tool_call_counts (30 lines). Parsing JSONL event logs, computing per-player costs/thinking time/tool call counts.\n\n3. **export_errors.py** (~100 lines) — _read_errors (40 lines), _is_llm_error, _link_errors_to_decisions. Error log extraction and classification.\n\n4. **export_decisions.py** (~300 lines) — _build_decisions and related snapshot/action building logic. Constructing canonical decision objects from game events + LLM events.\n\nThe remaining core (~500 lines) would keep: build_export, export_game, read_game_winner, _read_server_events, deck helpers, tournament detection, and main.",
